// EZ Minutes tunebook index — bundled with the suite, loaded by both capture.html and
// compile.html via <script src="tunebook-index.js">. This file is intentionally separate
// from the apps themselves: it can be edited or replaced independently (a newer version
// with more books, corrected pages, etc.) without touching any app code, and neither app
// ever fetches or checks for updates automatically — whatever is sitting next to the HTML
// files at load time is simply what's used.
//
// To add a tunebook: add an entry under EZ_MINUTES_TUNEBOOKS.books, keyed by a short
// internal code (used internally and in the CSV's Book column — pick something that won't
// collide with an existing one). Then add a line to TUNEBOOK-CHANGELOG.md recording what was
// added and when.
//
// Book entry shape:
//   fullTitle    — the book's full published title (required)
//   commonName   — a short display name for the Capture checkbox/badge (required)
//   singloudCode — SingLoud.org's short work code for this book, if known (optional, "" if not)
//   shmhaCode    — the SHMHA Minutes Book abbreviation for this book, if known (optional, "" if not)
//   badgeColor     — background color for this book's badge/pill in Capture's UI, as any
//                    valid CSS color (optional; falls back to a neutral gray if omitted)
//   badgeTextColor — text color to pair with badgeColor (optional, same fallback rule)
//                    Both are cosmetic, book-specific data (typically matched to the book's
//                    real cover color) and belong here rather than as a growing list of
//                    hardcoded CSS classes in capture.html, one per book — the same reason
//                    everything else in this file lives here instead of in the apps.
//   isSacredHarpDefault — true only for the book(s) that are the tradition's unspoken
//                    baseline (currently SHM1991 and SHM2025). Downstream of one fact
//                    about a book, this drives two related behaviors together: it's
//                    preferred as a singing's "default book" even over one used more often,
//                    and it never gets its own SHMHA code, since SHMHA's code system exists
//                    to flag departures from the baseline, not to identify the baseline
//                    itself. Omit entirely for every other book (do not set to false).
//   addedIn      — the suite version this book was first included in (for the changelog)
//   songs        — { "<page><t|b if split>": { title: "<title as printed in the book>" } }
//                  Split top/bottom pages are two separate keys (e.g. "45t" and "45b").
//                  Whether a bare page number is a split page is derived automatically from
//                  whether both "<N>t" and "<N>b" keys exist — there's no separate list to
//                  keep in sync. A song entry is a small object (not a bare string) so more
//                  fields can be added later — composer, meter, first line, etc. — without
//                  another breaking change to this format.

